```
ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: red
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS:
  - CIRCULARITY: references are GENERATED by a mixture of (salience + repeat + recency)
    with weights w_sal, w_rep, w_rec; the EC predictor is GIVEN exactly those three
    features (salience observable, repeat history, recency). Top-k by the generative
    parameters is by construction near-optimal — the "oracle gap = [0,0] in
    favorable regime" is a TAUTOLOGY of the trace model, not evidence about real
    attention signal. "Predictability=high" literally means "most reference mass is
    explained by the features EC consumes."
  - RT is rigged to lose: warmup=5 + repeat-reference bias guarantees old spans keep
    being re-cited, so dropping-oldest must miss them. This is a property of the
    generative process, not of real agent transcripts.
  - "task-success" = referenced-span PRESENCE; this is the LOSS the EC scorer
    optimizes (keep spans likely to be referenced). It is not task accuracy; it is
    self-evaluation of the retention objective.
  - SPAN_LEN=32 is BOTH the compression atom AND the reference atom — no
    boundary/fragmentation cost. Real systems must guess span boundaries.
CONFOUNDS:
  - EC consumes the TRUE latent salience (the generative parameter), not a noisy
    estimate; real attention/citation signal is a noisy, model/layer-dependent
    proxy. Effect size of EC is inflated by zero-noise observability.
  - "Tool-result-specific" angle (the claimed distinct contribution) is NOT tested
    — the simulation appends generic verbose spans; nothing about the trace makes
    them tool outputs vs any other appended text. Whatever EC achieves here would
    apply equally to assistant prose, user messages, retrieved docs — the same as
    StreamingLLM/H2O/SnapKV operate on generic context.
  - No comparison against KV-eviction baselines (H2O, SnapKV) or prompt-compression
    baselines (LLMLingua) — only against the weakest RT strawman. The packet's own
    novelty_killer flags this and the L0 ignores it.
  - Reference probability includes recency as a generative term — so EC's recency
    feature partially leaks future structure, double-dipping with RT.
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED:
  - That real tool outputs have ref_density ∈ {0.02, 0.08, 0.25} structure at all
    (assumed by construction; the L0 cannot speak to it).
  - That real attention/citation predicts future references with high AUC on real
    traces (the entire crux; this L0 brackets, does not test).
  - That salience is OBSERVABLE pre-compression at zero cost (in practice computing
    attention mass over the full context is not free).
  - That spans are the right atom on real tool outputs (JSON fields? lines?
    paragraphs?) — boundary detection error not modeled.
  - That the predictability knob's "high" setting corresponds to anything realizable
    on real attention; it is an unnormalized mixing weight with no empirical anchor.
STATISTICAL_GAPS:
  - Only 8 seeds per cell. "wins 633/648 cells" treats (config × seed) as independent
    comparisons, inflating N by 8×; the per-config win count is what matters and is
    not reported with a per-config significance test.
  - Bootstrap CI "[0,0]" for the favorable-regime oracle gap almost certainly means
    ALL paired samples were exactly 0 (degenerate equality, not a tight estimate) —
    this is consistent with the tautology above and should be reported as such, not
    as a confidence statement.
  - No multiple-comparison correction across 81 configs; the broad "wins everywhere"
    claim is not adjusted.
  - Sensitivity to (w_rec, w_sal, w_rep, ref_rate, warmup) NOT swept. The whole
    result lives in a single point of the generative-parameter space.
  - No predictor-AUC reported — we cannot tell HOW MUCH past-signal predicts
    future references, only that EC > RT in this construction.
RATIONALE: This is a green-candidate on the basis of a control whose negative
  outcome was structurally impossible: EC is scored against a generative process
  parameterized by the very features EC consumes, with zero observation noise, and
  evaluated on a target (span presence) that IS the EC objective. The
  "make-or-break" oracle-gap=[0,0] finding follows from the trace model, not from a
  property of real attention or real tool outputs. The crowded-prior-art sweep
  (LLMLingua/H2O/SnapKV) is OWED by the packet's own admission and absent. The
  tool-result-specific angle (the only claimed distinct contribution) is not
  operationalized in the simulation at all. Per the orchestrator caveat: sparsity
  + predictability are assumed by construction and realizability is bracketed —
  exactly the two load-bearing assumptions. RED until a real-attention/real-task
  pass closes them, or until at minimum the L0 adds (i) noisy salience observable,
  (ii) span-boundary mismatch, (iii) H2O/SnapKV-style baselines, (iv) generative-
  parameter sensitivity sweep, (v) predictor-AUC reporting.
```
